# Files graphify must not treat as source (PLAN-GRAPHIFY §P0).
#
# .gitignore is merged in automatically and already covers dist/ and
# node_modules/. What it does NOT cover is the generated payloads the plugin
# COMMITS on purpose: `npm run build:plugin` bundles the CLI into bin/scale.mjs
# and copies the built web app into web-dist/, and both are checked in so the
# plugin stays self-contained (README "Architecture").
#
# Left in, those two files supplied 1418 of 2103 nodes (67%) on the first
# extraction — a bundled copy of code that is already in the graph via its real
# sources, which would double-count every symbol and swamp every metric.

packages/plugin/bin/
packages/plugin/web-dist/

# graphify's own output, so a re-extraction never reads its previous run.
graphify-out/
